In professional embedded development, knowing how to find information in documentation is just as 
important as writing code. 

1. Datasheet (DS): 
Use it when you need to know (Think: What can this chip physically do?):
a. Pin assignments and alternate functions
b. Supply voltage and electrical limits
c. Package dimensions
d. Memory size and device specifications

2. Reference Manual
Use it when you need to know (THink: How do I control the hardware?)
a. Which registers control a peripheral
b. Which bits enable or configure hardware
c. How timers, GPIO, UART, ADC, and DMA work
d. Which clock enables a peripheral


